{"title":"2000 AIME I Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A container in the shape of a right circular <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cone\" title=\"Cone\">cone</a> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> inches tall and its base has a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-inch <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Radius\" title=\"Radius\">radius</a>. The liquid that is sealed inside is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> inches deep when the cone is held with its <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Point\" title=\"Point\">point</a> down and its base horizontal. When the liquid is held with its point up and its base horizontal, the height of the liquid is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/8/1586f2bca69882cdcb09b653822a61d6a5931db7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m - n\\sqrt [3]{p},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" /> from the base where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/d/1ed17364b06ad42c2450df4d0f6a0f06034086bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"13\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/4/c54e7152acd659788861f0453ac195c635e0a005.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are positive integers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is not divisible by the cube of any prime number. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/2/8f23423034093484df72a3171da00744b1e11963.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m + n + p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"80\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2000_I_AIME-8.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/5/53/2000_I_AIME-8.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"472\" height=\"351\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The scale factor is uniform in all dimensions, so the volume of the liquid is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/8/a586457f7b06a36e87c1274979fa96b737bc4ddb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right)^{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"49\" height=\"48\" /> of the container. The remaining section of the volume is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/5/ae522b801bb9a1f482f98ddf4bca6b323212d703.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1-\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right)^{3}}{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"71\" height=\"46\" /> of the volume, and therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/d/82d833e9578ca67e722e07e7746689660b37bec8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\left(1-\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right)^{3}\\right)^{1/3}}{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"110\" height=\"56\" /> of the height when the vertex is at the top.\n</p><p>So, the liquid occupies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/f/cef360553d4d5e8ba57e0c04bc90bd86ee349cbe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1-\\left(1-\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right)^{3}\\right)^{1/3}}{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"141\" height=\"56\" /> of the height, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/6/c66b41a07cdb71ce409594ab98bcddb724b19658.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12-12\\left(1-\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right)^{3}\\right)^{1/3}=12-3\\left(37^{1/3}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"318\" height=\"57\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/e/cde3e3ecd24b68c72768dc2986e3dd5ca3fb5dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n+p=\\boxed{052}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"143\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>(Computational) The volume of a cone can be found by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/e/45ef4d79a63042ca5b98ee817e99cda99cf5a556.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V = \\frac{\\pi}{3}r^2h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"80\" height=\"33\" />. In the second container, if we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/e/beecf0384713507f16489323b5600ccece5d52d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h&#39;,r&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"35\" height=\"17\" /> represent the height, radius (respectively) of the air (so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/f/48f7f365e6fc0d56bff1d7f685b52d66d95a5fac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 -h&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" /> is the height of the liquid), then the volume of the liquid can be found by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/0/c90d0851730993fadf7da277c30abf2971317664.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{3}r^2h - \\frac{\\pi}{3}(r&#39;)^2h&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"128\" height=\"33\" />. \n</p><p>By <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Similar_triangle&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Similar triangle (page does not exist)\">similar triangles</a>, we find that the dimensions of the liquid in the first cone to the entire cone is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/1/e1150a17bf1b733cb666be84d920c71fc96bb3f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"38\" />, and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/c/64c2064b4e575ac0de2ead798ab479264cc86a81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r&#39; = \\frac{rh&#39;}{h}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"63\" height=\"38\" />; equating,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/a/14ab28bada1a2faa03eb79845b8e1cef3c8a0d39.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\left(\\frac{3}{4}r\\right)^2 \\left(\\frac{3}{4}h\\right) &amp;= \\frac{\\pi}{3}\\left(r^2h - \\left(\\frac{rh&#39;}{h}\\right)^2h&#39;\\right)\\\\ \\frac{37}{64}r^2h &amp;= \\frac{r^2}{h^2}(h&#39;)^3 \\\\ h&#39; &amp;= \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{37}{64} \\cdot 12^3} = 3\\sqrt[3]{37}\\end{align*}\" width=\"319\" height=\"149\" />\n</p><p>Thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/e/9cefade80e75d0a63439935c0016c5ed094a047c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 - h&#39; = 12-3\\sqrt[3]{37}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"163\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/e/cde3e3ecd24b68c72768dc2986e3dd5ca3fb5dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n+p=\\boxed{052}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"143\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>From the formula <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/1/d415abf8bd3bc80f57e924afd1a221309dee553e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V=\\frac{\\pi r^2h}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"79\" height=\"39\" />, we can find that the volume of the container is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/3/b034b5cee39a45fc8e259a06f15941013320075f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"37\" height=\"13\" />. The cone formed by the liquid is similar to the original, but scaled down by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/1/e1150a17bf1b733cb666be84d920c71fc96bb3f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"38\" /> in all directions, so its volume is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/f/41fcf64805e2787595e136453c99f2efa3809eda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100\\pi*\\frac{27}{64}=\\frac{675\\pi}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"142\" height=\"38\" />. The volume of the air in the container is the volume of the container minus the volume of the liquid, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/3/08365b2b088ee05ceb461e5a8da9a8bbc230691c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{925\\pi}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"40\" height=\"38\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/2/5c2659de9a6b852058680fa15e3a6b27aa9700d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{37}{64}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" /> of the volume of the container. When the point faces upwards, the air forms a cone at the top of the container. This cone must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/0/5c0b3614fefdff1c70177f558542613489d652fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{37}{64}}=\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{37}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"101\" height=\"43\" /> of the height of the container. This means that the height of the liquid is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/c/89c79cfc4c11df781ee4e63fac65b45578b24130.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12\\left(1-\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{37}}{4}\\right)=12-3\\sqrt[3]{37}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"226\" height=\"53\" /> inches, so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/7/9c7fb4bc8d49a4c3b1f0991b29e1a9d2a39b7cf2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{052}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />. Solution by Zeroman\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We find that the volume of the cone is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/3/b034b5cee39a45fc8e259a06f15941013320075f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"37\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p>The volume of the cone with height 9 is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/5/165d975c98823a2ab4a107297cbf8f4a080f897a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{675}{16}\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"44\" height=\"38\" />. \n</p><p>The difference between the two volumes is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/c/e4c3579c72b8a30a7e9f666d757bcafda9b73e4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{925}{16}\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"44\" height=\"38\" />. Note that this is the volume of the cone essentially 'on top of' the frustum described in the problem when the liquid is held with the base horizontal. \n</p><p>We can express the volume as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/e/33e71adc986dcf1ed2eb6159e2d18a39568f3950.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2\\pi\\cdot\\frac{12}{5}x\\cdot\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"103\" height=\"38\" />, where x is the radius of the cone. \n</p><p>Solving this equation, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/5/ad5ff51e5ab1d6c8188a502e9acba485538df801.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{5\\sqrt[3]{37}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"83\" height=\"43\" />. The height of this cone is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/f/85f448517195cbdc424948dcb01df3282f099092.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{12}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> of the radius. \n</p><p>Then we subtract the value from the height, 12, to get our answer: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/e/41e17c2bc78b5befebb998d42dfa04bce1bfb779.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12-3\\sqrt[3]{37}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"21\" />. \n</p><p>Therefore, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/c/7acf4a71988f7d6f49dfca448ebbd1e36f9ef83c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12+3+37=\\boxed{52}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"145\" height=\"25\" />. ~MC413551\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I\" title=\"2000 AIME I\">2000 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2000 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2000 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2000\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2000 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2000 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2000 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2000 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2000 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2000 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2000 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2000 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2000 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2000 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2000 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2000 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2000 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2000 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2000 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2000 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017095158\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.041 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.061 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 297/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1786/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 108/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8150/5000000 bytes\n-->\n